# Analects Book 18 (微子). Same format as the pilot (drafts/analects-01/units.py): one unit per stretch
# between Zhu Xi's commentary interruptions (28 units, 11 passages; lemma 28, the running head 論語卷九, is
# skipped by the build). One file (the book is short); UNITS[0] is lemma 0.
# Token format as the pilot:
#   tokens separated by " | "; a token is  CHARS[PUNCT][=pinyin][/context gloss[//char gloss//char gloss]]
#   a leading "^" breaks the verse line before the token.
# Punctuation is editorial (the edition has none) and always trails the word before it.
# Pinyin defaults to the glossary's first reading; every polyphone states its reading here, and so does
# every bound compound and every character not yet in the glossary (on every occurrence).
# Passages follow Zhu Xi's chapter breaks (heading: 此篇多記聖賢之出處凡十一章; each ○ checked in the commentary
# file KR1h0015_008.txt): 18.1 = units 0–1, 18.2 = 2, 18.3 = 3, 18.4 = 4, 18.5 = 5–6, 18.6 = 7–10,
# 18.7 = 11–15, 18.8 = 16–20, 18.9 = 21–25 (one chapter: Zhu Xi 此記賢人之隠遁以附前章), 18.10 = 26, 18.11 = 27.
# Each stretch holds at most one chapter (no npas).
# Line breaks: the lines of t (one more than the ^ breaks after the first token) equal the lines of l in
# every unit. Speech openers (子曰：「, 丈人曰：「 …) stand on a line of their own when the speech runs to more
# than one line. Quotation marks balance within every unit. Where a speech runs on past one of Zhu Xi's
# comments the continuation is left unquoted, Chinese and English alike (as Book 17): 18.8 unit 20 (我則異於是
# 無可無不可, the Master's words under the 子曰 of unit 17; it opens its unit and has no verb of saying, so
# it stands unquoted and the note says whose words they are, as 17.21 unit 46). Units 18 and 19 open with
# the narrator's 謂 'of X (he said)' and quote their own words, balanced within the unit. A token cannot
# begin with a mark, so 「 trails the name before it (少連：「, 夷逸：「). Exchanges keep one 曰 per line
# (18.6 units 8–9).
# Cross-references cite the shipped passage numbers: 殷 the Yin (2.23); 栁下惠 Liuxia Hui (15.13); 齊景公 (12.11,
#   16.12); 季氏 (3.1, 16.1); Ji Huanzi (17.1 note); 歸 guī 'to send as a gift' (17.1); 鳳 the phoenix (9.8);
#   辟 bì = 避 (14.39); 晨門 and 荷蕢, the other recluses (14.41, 14.42); 仲由 Zhong You (6.6); 丘 Qiu (7.23,
#   16.1); 隠居 (16.11); 天下有道 (8.13, 16.2); 如之何 (2.20); 伯夷 叔齊 Boyi and Shuqi (5.22, 7.14, 16.12);
#   仲雍 Zhongyong with Taibo (8.1); 權 (9.29); 大師 tài shī (3.23); 師摯 Music Master Zhi (8.15); 自衛反魯 (9.14);
#   磬 the chime-stones (14.42); 周公 (7.5); 故舊 (8.2); 大臣 (11.23); 求備 (13.25); 适 kuò (14.6, 南宫适).
# Repeats and shipped English kept: 孔子 'Kongzi' throughout (as Books 16–17); 夫子 fū zǐ 'the Master' (10) and
#   'my master', 'your master' in Zilu's and the old man's mouths (11); 子路 Zilu; 仲由 'Zhong You'; 栁下惠 'Liuxia
#   Hui' (2, 16, 18; 15.13's gloss); 齊景公 'Duke Jing of Qi' (3); 季氏 'the Ji' (3); 伯夷 'Boyi', 叔齊 'Shuqi' (16,
#   17); 天下 'all under Heaven / the world' with 有道 'has the Way' (10; 16.2); 辟 bì 'avoid' (6, 9; 14.39);
#   荷 hè 'shouldering' (11; 14.42); 隠 / 居 unbound 'living hidden' (19; 16.11); 大師 'the Grand Music-Master'
#   (21; 3.23); 擊 jī 磬 qìng 'striking the chime-stones' (25; 14.42); 周公 'the Duke of Zhou'; 故舊 'old
#   associates' (26; 8.2); 大臣 'great ministers' (26; 11.23); 求 / 備 unbound 'demand everything' (26; 13.25);
#   如之何 'how' (15); 君子 'the gentleman'; 鳥獸 unbound 'birds and beasts' (10; 17.9).
