#   chime-stones' describe what each man did (Zhu Xi 鼓擊鼓者; 播搖也) and are not bound.
# New bound keys needed (pinyin as stated):
#   微子 (wēi zǐ — the Viscount of Wei: elder half-brother of Zhou 紂, last king of the Shang; Zhu Xi 微箕二國名子爵
#     也微子紂庶兄; Ma Rong in He Yan 微子紂之庶兄)
#   箕子 (jī zǐ — the Viscount of Ji: an uncle of Zhou, imprisoned and made a slave; Zhu Xi 箕子比干紂諸父)
#   比干 (bǐ gān — Bi Gan: an uncle of Zhou, killed for remonstrating; He Yan's text 比于 in the lemma)
#   士師 (shì shī — officer of justice, in charge of trials and prisons; Zhu Xi 士師獄官; Kong Anguo 典獄之官)
